FINAL ANSWER:
No active owner exists for `lib/index.js`. Every author with lines in the file has been inactive for more than 6 months, counted from 2026-04-22. The tool flags the file as orphaned.

**Blame is misleading here.** Fiona Formatter owns 89.9% of the lines, but only because of the reformat commit `62628c0` (2026-04-12, 214 lines added and 214 deleted). I wouldn't treat them as the domain expert. Use `git blame -w` or the file history to find who wrote the logic.

**Candidates by real knowledge of the file:**
- **Troy Goode** wrote the original file in 2013 and has the most substantive commits. Their last commit was 2026-04-10 (`b2005d9`, "annotate handlers"). They are the best match for the overall design, but they have no commits since 2026-04-22.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** made the Vary-header, options-delegate and frozen-options fixes in 2017. That is the edge-case logic most likely to break. Their last commit in the repo was 2021-09-07, so they are inactive too.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** wrote the origin handling for regexps and arrays in 2015. That is also the most complex part of the file.

**Recommendation:**
1. Ask Troy Goode first if they can still be reached. They know the file best and committed to it recently.
2. If you change Vary headers, preflight handling or `options.origin` matching, have someone review the matching tests in `test/`. The tests are the only remaining record of the 2015–2017 edge-case fixes. Commit `02afce3` ("vary header coverage") touched them recently.
3. If nobody can review it, run the full test suite and compare the response headers before and after your change.

I only looked at git history. I can't see CODEOWNERS or who is currently active on the project outside this repo. Tell me which part of the file you're changing and I can narrow this down.

